      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the 5.5 to 7.0 pH range, iron and manganese become optimally bioavailable for grapevines, as these micronutrients exhibit peak solubility in slightly acidic to neutral soils. However, as pH rises toward 7.0, the chemical solubility of these elements declines significantly, increasing the risk of micronutrient deficiency even when total soil concentrations remain high. Consequently, vineyard management in this range often requires careful monitoring and targeted foliar or root-zone applications to prevent iron and manganese deficiency, particularly as soils approach neutrality.",
